+/// The size of a pooled block, at most the device's `maxMemoryAllocationSize`. SweetMetal2: 8 MB, not 64: `dedicated`
+/// triggers past `block_bytes / 2` (4 MB), so 11.5 MB full-screen render targets get blocks of their own, freed with them.
+/// With 24 MB blocks a small long-lived resource pinned a block that two render targets had used: backboardd held
+/// 18-26 such blocks (430-620 MB of the GPU pool, vayu log35) and iOS jetsammed a process a second.
+pub(super) const BLOCK_BYTES: u64 = 8 << 20;
 
